WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:05.480
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm explaining the shocking ending

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:09.520
of The Invisible Man, and the thrilling twists
and clues that led to that big moment.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:13.490
Plus, I'll reveal how the finale connects
to the new Invisible Woman film.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:17.450
Spoilers, of course, for the movie, so take
care if you haven't seen it yet.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:21.980
The film's first jaw-dropping surprise happens
when Cecilia is at dinner with her sister,

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:26.950
Emily and out of nowhere the Invisible Man
slashes Emily's throat and pins the murder

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:29.750
on Cee by placing the knife in her hand.

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:34.660
Leading up to this, Adrian has been slowly
making Cecilia look and feel crazy, first

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:39.190
faking his own death, then stalking and terrorising
her at her friend's house.

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:43.380
One of the first big clues foreshadowing Emily's
murder comes when Cecilia is alone in the

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:47.780
house with The Invisible Man, and she decides
to call Adrian's cell phone which buzzes from

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.140
the attic above.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:53.600
Cee climbs up and after finding the phone
together with a large kitchen knife, a text

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:56.610
message pops up with the single word "SURPRISE".

00:00:56.610 --> 00:01:00.680
She can't figure out why there's a knife there,
but the sign that it's a future murder weapon

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:04.170
is how it's already bagged like it's a piece
of evidence.

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:08.100
When she's later locked up and drugged in
a mental hospital for the crime and what everyone

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:13.689
thinks are her delusional ravings, an invisible
Adrian whispers "surprise", tormenting her

00:01:13.689 --> 00:01:16.030
that he had this moment planned all along.

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:20.959
The word, and idea of, "surprise" pays off
in an even bigger way in the movie's final

00:01:20.959 --> 00:01:21.959
twist.

00:01:21.959 --> 00:01:25.709
When Cee goes to have dinner with Adrian,
he still thinks he's in control and tells

00:01:25.709 --> 00:01:28.520
her
"I know you better than anyone else in the

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:31.389
world;
that shouldn't come as a... surprise."

00:01:31.389 --> 00:01:37.509
The way Adrian pauses, smiles, and then emphasises
the word "surprise" is his way of letting

00:01:37.509 --> 00:01:42.029
her know that it was indeed him who killed
her sister and has been torturing her, not

00:01:42.029 --> 00:01:43.329
just his brother.

00:01:43.329 --> 00:01:47.990
His constant denials at the dinner table prior
to this are yet another example of how he

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:49.380
gaslights her.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:55.069
And so, sick of his continued abuse, Cecilia
excuses herself to the bathroom, then off-camera

00:01:55.069 --> 00:02:00.759
sneaks into the bedroom closet where she recovers
the invisibility suit she hid there earlier.

00:02:00.759 --> 00:02:05.149
Invisible now, she walks back to the dinner
table and, aware of the security cameras,

00:02:05.149 --> 00:02:09.860
makes him slit his own throat, mirroring the
way he killed her sister.

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:14.900
As he dies, she whispers the word "Surprise!"
showing that she's turned his own tricks back

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:15.920
on him.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:20.840
By the way, notice how Cecilia decided they
eat steak, rather than the sushi or pasta

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:24.840
she was also offered, for dinner, so that
Adrian would be holding the knife she needed

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:26.030
to kill him.

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:30.300
And a clue that Cee would decide to wear the
invisibility suit against Adrian was hinted

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:34.990
at in the hospital on a poster titled "You
don't have to face yourself alone".

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:40.890
The poster features two silhouetted figures,
and while it's obviously aimed at people with

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:46.250
mental health issues, maybe bipolar for example,
it also plays on the idea of Cee using an

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:51.320
alternate invisible persona to deal with Adrian
as well as the fact that we soon discover

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:54.040
that a second man donned the invisible suit.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:58.630
Indeed, doubles and mirrors are a recurring
theme in the movie, with Cecilia seeing a

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:02.700
reflection of herself in the bathroom mirror
just before she puts the invisible suit on

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:03.740
to kill Adrian.

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:08.050
And part of the set-up for Cecilia hiding
the second invisibility suit in the bedroom

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:12.140
closet comes in the scene where she goes for
a job interview and the interviewer says

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:13.940
"we both know the value of closet space".

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:14.940
The comment refers to him starting his company
in a supply closet as well as Cecilia's time

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:15.940
in Paris when she stayed in an apartment as
small as a broom closet.

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:18.770
Which points forward to the film's finale,
as well as back to the start of the movie

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:22.250
where Cee hid a go-bag in her closet to help
her escape Adrian.

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:27.640
As we discover in another twist, Adrian's
brother Tom was also his accomplice, helping

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:30.830
him fake his own death, and even once wearing
the suit.

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:33.690
Tom claimed he'd been controlled by Adrian
all his life.

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:38.400
And while that may be true, he still lied
to Cecilia, feeding her false information,

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.460
essentially gaslighting her as well.

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:44.370
"Only thing more brilliant than inventing
something that makes you invisible is not

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.180
inventing it, and making you think he did."

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:50.690
When Cee tells Tom he's just a 'jellyfish
version of his brother', she means he lacks

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:55.340
a spine, but the fact that jellyfish are known
for their translucent or transparent look

00:03:55.340 --> 00:04:00.380
means it's also an intriguing nod to the fact
that Tom will later wear the invisible suit.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:04.430
Tom was always quite shady from the start
knowing things he shouldn't, such as where

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:05.540
Cee was living.

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:09.770
Remember she received the letter about Adrian's
will at James's house, probably because when

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:14.440
Emily saw the news about his death, she ignored
Cee's instructions not to go there and Adrian

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:17.590
was tracking or watching her, just as Cee
predicted.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:21.900
Tom also knew Cee had set up a bank account
for Sydney's college fund, again something

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:23.129
that should be private.

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:27.680
Most likely is that while Adrian was stalking
Cecilia and breaking in to her laptop, he

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:32.120
was keeping tabs on her and relaying the info
back to his brother.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:36.409
As the saying goes, the greatest trick the
devil ever pulled was convincing the world

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:41.419
he didn't exist, an idea that perfectly fits
the character of the Invisible Man.

00:04:41.419 --> 00:04:45.150
Even at the end of the movie, Adrian pretends
he was never the Invisible Man and that it

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:48.860
was his brother Tom who was responsible for
everything that happened.

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:54.100
Adrian flips the truth so far that he even
claims he's the victim and that Tom was controlling

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:55.100
him.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:58.669
The movie's writer-director Leigh Whannell
has said that Adrian's emotional intelligence

00:04:58.669 --> 00:05:03.550
and charm is a classic trait of narcissists
and sociopaths who he describes as "scientists

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:08.039
of the human condition [who] can break someone
down very quickly, assess their needs and

00:05:08.039 --> 00:05:09.809
desires, and play to that."

00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:12.139
Which is why Adrian is good at reading people.

00:05:12.139 --> 00:05:16.650
For example, when they were still together,
he figured out without her even saying a word,

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:18.189
that she wanted to leave him.

00:05:18.189 --> 00:05:24.479
And his reaction was that of a sociopath:
"Wherever you go, I'll be standing right behind

00:05:24.479 --> 00:05:25.479
you.

00:05:25.479 --> 00:05:28.370
I know you better than anyone else in the
world."

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:32.550
When Cecilia was wearing a wire at the end
and trying to get him to confess, you could

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:36.830
sense he probably knew what she was doing,
and on top of wanting to gaslight her as usual,

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:40.990
that was another reason he refused to admit
anything openly.

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:45.150
Likewise his comment that 'you're the only
person in the world who gets to see my hand

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:49.999
shake' was a tactic to let her know that only
she knows the truth about him and no one else

00:05:49.999 --> 00:05:51.289
would believe her.

00:05:51.289 --> 00:05:55.439
He also knew she was taking birth control
pills in secret so switched them out behind

00:05:55.439 --> 00:06:00.530
her back, essentially drugging her so she'd
get pregnant, quite likely with Diazepam given

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:02.620
the very high level of it in her blood.

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:07.780
As Cecilia unwittingly continues to take the
drugs, Adrian breaks into her email, sending

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:11.849
a threatening, incriminating message from
her to her sister, which later provides the

00:06:11.849 --> 00:06:14.069
motive for Emily's murder.

00:06:14.069 --> 00:06:18.370
Adrian is constantly isolating Cee from the
few people already in her life as well as

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:20.940
any new people she comes into contact with.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:25.499
He also sabotages her job interview that could
make her financially independent of his money

00:06:25.499 --> 00:06:28.189
by emptying her portfolio.

00:06:28.189 --> 00:06:32.819
And he later puts those architect plans that
he took in the attic, together with the kitchen

00:06:32.819 --> 00:06:35.559
knife, taunting her about what he can do to
her.

00:06:35.559 --> 00:06:40.659
He also sees himself as an amazing god-like
figure, the master of everyone and everything

00:06:40.659 --> 00:06:41.749
around him.

00:06:41.749 --> 00:06:46.099
When they were a couple, he was such a control
freak that he decided everything Cecilia did,

00:06:46.099 --> 00:06:47.770
wore and said.

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:52.020
Even his dog Zeus wears a shock collar with
tech of Adrian's own design.

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:54.400
And let's talk about the name he chose for
that dog:

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:59.770
the ancient Greek deity Zeus is the king of
all the other gods and men, which again highlights

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:03.979
how Adrian imagines himself as the supreme
master and god of all.

00:07:03.979 --> 00:07:08.290
And it's no coincidence that the location
of Adrian's house is Celestial Drive.

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:14.270
As a genius inventor, Adrian uses his invisibility
technology to psychologically and physically

00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:18.949
terrorise Cecilia and those around her, to
make her appear unhinged and, ultimately,

00:07:18.949 --> 00:07:20.439
drive her back to him.

00:07:20.439 --> 00:07:24.789
When Cee asks The Invisible Man why he cares
about her, when with his wealth and power

00:07:24.789 --> 00:07:29.400
he could have almost anyone, the answer that
Tom later gives her is that Adrian needs her

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:33.400
because she doesn't need him, and that nobody's
ever left him before.

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:36.699
Whannell has said that when he was writing
his first draft of the movie, he felt that

00:07:36.699 --> 00:07:41.599
the themes "of gaslighting, domestic abuse
and not being believed or feeling like there's

00:07:41.599 --> 00:07:46.649
an unseen threat" would perfectly fit a modern
version of the classic invisible man villain.

00:07:46.649 --> 00:07:50.699
And Whannell went on to say that "the horror
genre lends itself to depicting the worst

00:07:50.699 --> 00:07:55.349
of society's problems because it can illustrate
our collective fears.

00:07:55.349 --> 00:07:58.759
Cecilia's character is an example of what
it's like for a woman to be driven to feel

00:07:58.759 --> 00:08:03.479
'crazy' in the wake of abuse when no one around
you believes what you're saying."

00:08:03.479 --> 00:08:08.960
Ultimately, as Cee couldn't make Adrian admit
his guilt, the legal options for getting justice

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:12.759
weren't available, so he would have continued
to terrorise her as the Invisible Man if she

00:08:12.759 --> 00:08:14.180
didn't stay with him.

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:18.499
Which is why Whannell says that with the ending,
he decided "to give [Cecilia] some catharsis,

00:08:18.499 --> 00:08:20.490
[as he] wanted [her] to feel free."

00:08:20.490 --> 00:08:26.330
And so, as Cee walks out of Adrian's house,
free at last, we can see from her open bag

00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:30.479
that she's still got her invisibility suit,
meaning she could easily be in a sequel or

00:08:30.479 --> 00:08:34.380
possibly in Universal's The Invisible Woman
movie which is already in development with

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:37.310
Elizabeth Banks directing and starring as
the title character.

00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:41.810
I wonder if the film will feature Banks donning
the suit and using it to violently deal with

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:44.750
people who've evaded justice such as abusers.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:48.910
After all, according to The Hollywood Reporter,
the tone of the new film is "Thelma &amp; Louise

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:50.750
meets American Psycho".

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:54.590
Although Universal have abandoned their Dark
Universe which was going to connect their

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:59.371
catalogue of classic monsters, it seems there's
potential for some sort of crossover, even

00:08:59.371 --> 00:09:03.050
a very small one, if the studio did decide
it wants to make it happen.

00:09:03.050 --> 00:09:07.920
If they did choose to connect the two movies,
then Cecilia could, for example, supply Banks's

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:11.950
Invisible Woman with the tech for the suit
or they could even team up.

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:17.150
Either way, as Cecilia shows in The Invisible
Man, stalking is a very real danger in real

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:18.960
life and online.

